name issue_151_outage_3s_v2
describe 3 s outage with all v2 switches on: the receiver stops NACKing what a keyframe made moot (issue #151)
cc v2
pacer v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
seed 1
duration 30s
at 0s  capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
at 12s down
at 15s up
reverse at 0s delay=30ms
reverse at 12s down
reverse at 15s up
# Receiver NACK give-up (issue #151). Before the fix the receiver re-requested the ~60 packets lost in the outage
# every 20 ms for 2 s after the keyframe had been decoded (100 NACK batches, 47 useless retransmissions that
# queued behind the recovery keyframe); libwebrtc's NackRequester::ClearUpTo drops them at the first continuous
# frame (one burst, 17 RTX).
# Seeds 1-3 on main 3179f13: repair.overhead_pct 1.44 / 1.75 / 1.61, video.freeze_total_ms 4093 / 4084 / 4118;
# with the fix 1.34 / 1.37 / 1.33 and 4070 / 4034 / 4072.
# Target (issue #151): cc.queue_p95_ms < 40 (libwebrtc 39), freeze total within the parity band of libwebrtc (3217).
# The queue part is recorded as an explained difference (Owner, 2026-10-20; tools/catalog.py 5.11): seeds 1-10 on
# main 0b45569 give 64.2 vs 40.6 ms, a phase race over which frame the congestion window drops first after `up`.
expect repair.overhead_pct < 1.4
# No outage monitor under cc v2 and feedback handled before the capture in each test bench tick (#151): seed 1
# freeze 4089 -> 3229 ms (libwebrtc 3221), repair 1.38 -> 0.10 % (0.58), longest audio gap 3550 -> 2980 ms (2977).
# Known remaining (seeds 1-10 on main 70e20a7 with this change): seeds 2 and 3 still lose the race, freeze 4666 / 3948
# ms and repair 6.30 / 3.18 % (main 4067 / 4047 and 1.43 / 1.26; libwebrtc 3256 / 3175 and 0.36 / 0.53). Their
# decode-time-out PLI reaches the sender before the next capture, so that frame becomes the keyframe before the NACK
# arrives; libwebrtc's PLI lands after it on every traced seed. That follows from the frame release time
# (FrameDecodeTiming), receive timing owned by #24.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 3300
expect audio.longest_interruption_ms < 3000
